    <p>
      I'm <strong class="text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 font-semibold">Soumil Seal</strong>, a software developer and Bachelor of Computer Applications (BCA) undergraduate student based in India.
    </p>
    <p>
      My interest in software engineering began with curiosity about how large distributed web services remain fast and dependable under heavy concurrency. That curiosity led me from basic algorithmic scripts in C and Python to designing full-stack systems, containerized cloud pipelines, and developer tooling.
    </p>
    <p>
      Today, my focus centers on <span class="text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 font-medium">software engineering, backend systems, and cloud infrastructure</span>. I enjoy dissecting runtime mechanics—whether that's understanding how the V8 engine manages microtask queues, how containers coordinate through Linux cgroups, or how relational database query planners optimize multi-table joins.
    </p>
    <p>
      Outside of university coursework and software development, I document my experiments on my blog, contribute to open-source software, and participate in technical communities.
    </p>
